WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.510
HANK: Good morning, John, it's Friday.

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:08.610
JOHN: Good morning, Hank, it is indeed Friday!
Yes! That was a poor high five. Poor.

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:11.240
Today's video comes to you in three parts.
Part one...

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.331
HANK: ...an announcement. Part two...

00:00:12.331 --> 00:00:14.549
JOHN: ...a challenge, and part three...

00:00:14.549 --> 00:00:15.759
HANK: ...another announcement.

00:00:15.759 --> 00:00:17.449
JOHN: That is different from the first announcement.

00:00:17.449 --> 00:00:22.400
Part one, an announcement. The 2010 Project
for Awesome is happening.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.529
HANK: It's on! You might remember in 2007
when John and I kind of realized that Nerdfighteria

00:00:25.529 --> 00:00:30.210
had become a pretty big deal, and we wanted
to do something with the power that Nerdfighteria

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.210
wields.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:36.789
JOHN: We decided to take over YouTube and
for one day, YouTube would not be about kittens

00:00:36.789 --> 00:00:41.530
on Roombas, or about giraffe love, it would
be about charity.

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:44.690
HANK: And now for three years straight, we've
been doing this very successfully, and it's

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:46.199
been getting bigger and bigger every year...

00:00:46.199 --> 00:00:50.160
JOHN: This year it's going to be the biggest
it has ever been.

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:51.160
HANK: By far.

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:54.960
JOHN: There's going to be a huge, epic live
show out of Los Angeles...

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.900
HANK: We just got off the phone with YouTube.
So YouTube's basically giving us the same

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:01.500
kind of treatment that like Conan O'Brien
and the president get where they're doing

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:04.110
a four hour live stream on YouTube.

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:06.299
JOHN: So there's going to be this big live
show, but there'll also be--&lt;elbows Hank&gt;

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:10.860
sorry...BAHHH! But there's also going to be
traditional P4A stuff, which means that hopefully,

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:15.890
all of you will upload amazing Project For
Awesome videos on December 17th. The thing

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:19.720
to do is to show us charities you care about
in action.

00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:22.950
HANK: And I know this might sound weird, but
it might involve you getting out of your chair.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:26.560
JOHN: You might have to leave your bedroom.
And that's not something either Hank or I

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:30.500
enjoy, and we are sympathetic to the fact
that it is no fun for you, but if it makes

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:35.439
for a better Project For Awesome video, it
therefore makes for a better universe. And

00:01:35.439 --> 00:01:36.710
so...get out there!

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:40.110
HANK: So we're giving you some lead time this
time, you have three weeks before December

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:44.329
17th to plan and execute your video. And we
will be announcing more things in the future,

00:01:44.329 --> 00:01:46.190
so give you subejuvevuv...

00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:50.380
JOHN: That was very eloquent, at the end particularly.
I'm moved.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:53.861
HANK: And we'll be giving you more details
as time goes on, like the thumbnail, and the

00:01:53.861 --> 00:01:56.020
logo, and the websites, and et cetera.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:58.159
JOHN: And for those of you who don't know
much about the Project For Awesome, you'll

00:01:58.159 --> 00:02:03.640
find videos here, here, here and here, and
you'll also find some videos in the dooblydoo.

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:05.229
HANK: Part two! A challenge!

00:02:05.229 --> 00:02:11.290
JOHN: We would like to challenge you, Nerdfighteria.
Last night at dinner, Hank and I were discussing

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:12.290
pasta.

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:13.290
HANK: Pasta and beef.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:18.050
JOHN: Everyone knows that it is far more efficient
in terms of energy output to create pasta

00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:22.880
than it is to create beef, and that remains
true even if you import the pasta from, say,

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:23.880
Italy...

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:26.550
HANK: But we were wondering, would this remain
true if you were importing the pasta from

00:02:26.550 --> 00:02:28.260
somewhere farther away. Say like the moon.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:29.260
JOHN: Like space.

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:33.050
HANK: So what we wanna know is, is it more
efficient to fly Apollo 11 to the moon, pick

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:38.360
up a load of pasta, fill up the capsule entirely
and then ship it back...would it then be more

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:43.061
energy intensive than growing a cow? Per calorie.
That is our question. We hope that there are

00:02:43.061 --> 00:02:46.650
some of you who are nerdy and smart enough
to give us an accurate answer.

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.700
JOHN: Because we couldn't figure it out.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:49.700
HANK: Nope!

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:54.000
JOHN: So we are turning to you, because you
never disappoint us. Nerdfighteria, if you

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:59.700
successfully determine for us whether moon
pasta is more efficient than earth beef, then

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:04.850
we will allow you to challenge us to do something
horrible. Part three...

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:07.930
HANK: The final announcement is that you may
have noticed that it is Black Friday. So in

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:11.040
the spirit of the holidays, DFTBA Records
is lowering prices on some new shirts and

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.750
some old favorites. Are you...putting bunny
ears...

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:14.420
JOHN: I was trying to but your head was too
high.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:16.920
HANK: The new shirts are the giraffe love
shirt--

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.400
JOHN: Why are the shirts on my face!

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:23.040
HANK: Because that's where they go! Two new
DFTBA shirts, which we're calling the DFTBA

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:26.600
University shirts, and the Giant Squid of
Anger shirt, designed by amazing nerdfighter

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:27.600
Vondell Swain.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:30.600
JOHN: Aaaghhhaaaagaaa! Alright so quick recap:

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:33.320
HANK: dftba.com/sale for all of your t-shirt
needs.

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:38.320
JOHN: Is it more efficient to have moon pasta
or earth burgers, and...

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:43.060
HANK: The Project for Awesome, December 17th,
get ready and be awesome. DFTBA, Nerdfighters,

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:44.070
he'll see you on Monday.

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:48.980
JOHN: ...I guess I'm Teller now.

